    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a more detailed explanation of quality gates for testing and staging:\n\n- **Automated Testing Quality Gate**: After automated tests run, implement a gate that prevents code from being reviewed or deployed if any automated tests fail. This ensures that any bugs or issues are addressed before the code reaches the review and deployment stages.\n\n- **Security Audit & Vulnerability Scan Quality Gate (Staging)**: Implement a gate that blocks deployment to production if any security vulnerabilities or high-severity issues are detected during the security audit and vulnerability scan. This helps prevent sensitive user data from being exposed in production.\n\n- **Performance and Quality Gate (Staging)**: Conduct a final performance test and quality gate before deployment. This gate checks metrics such as response rates, error rates, and system resource utilization to ensure the code meets the required performance standards.\n\nThese quality gates provide a final layer of assurance before code is deployed to production, helping ensure that it meets the required quality standards and is ready for deployment.",
      "source": "target",
